178	/// password auth (`createSession`) and app passwords. An OAuth session instead
179	/// carries a granular atproto scope string (e.g. `atproto transition:generic` or
180	/// `atproto repo:app.bsky.feed.post`); any such string maps to
181	/// [`AuthScope::Access`] so access-token-only routes can admit it, while route-level
182	/// permission checks inspect the raw scope claim for per-resource enforcement.

